WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.350
SAMIR DUTTA: My
name is Samir Dutta.

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.000
I'm a junior studying
computer science

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.350
and minoring in economics.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.149
And this past year I've been
working with the MIT Trade Lab

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:08.940
to apply machine learning
and data analysis

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.630
techniques in order
to try and figure out

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.180
trends in a database of
over 10 billion tariff rate

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.230
observations.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.690
So a few interesting
things to consider

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.090
is you can see in
these six graphs here,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.890
this is just for
six country pairs.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:25.170
You can see a lot of
variation in tariff rates,

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.830
and our goal was to
try and introduce

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.220
economic and political factors
into a machine learning model

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.930
to try to predict changes
in these tariff rates.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.830
Now, as you might expect,
economic and political

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.150
intuitions are qualitative.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.990
And in order to get accurate
machine learning models,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.850
you kind of need quantitative
continuous variables.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.520
And so a large part
of this project

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.840
was to take economic variables,
such as negotiation power,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.340
and quantify them into measures
that we can use in models.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.080
So for example, a
few facts that we

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.890
found were very
correlated and important

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.980
were the democratic
level of a country,

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.450
whether or not it's
in a trade war,

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.580
and how the health
of the economy

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.440
is doing relative
to previous years.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.200
And we were actually able to
use all these factors to develop

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.810
a model that had
over 80% accuracy

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.240
in predicting tariff rates.

